window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-0c31a6fce966b88c"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"run-codex-security-in-gitlab-cicd\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"gitlab-cicd-codex-security\">在 GitLab CI/CD 中运行 Codex Security</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p>在 GitLab CI/CD 中运行 Codex Security，扫描已提交的变更和受保护分支，将发现项发布到 GitLab Security，并可选择在草稿合并请求中提出已验证的修复。</p> <p>该工作流程会将扫描凭据与代码仓库写入权限分开。生成的变更在合并之前始终需要人工审核。</p> <p>建议从只报告扫描结果开始。只有在检查运行器、发现项和凭据边界后，才启用修复功能。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-begin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">开始之前</h2> <p>你需要：</p> <ul> <li>一个配置了可信运行器的 GitLab 项目；该运行器须支持 Codex 沙箱所需的用户命名空间。</li> <li>在 GitLab 项目中拥有 Maintainer 或 Owner 角色，以便配置<a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/ci/variables/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">项目 CI/CD 变量（需联网）</a>和受保护资源。</li> <li>一个具有 Codex Security 访问权限的 OpenAI API 密钥。使用 Platform API 密钥的组织可以<a href=\"https://openai.com/form/enterprise-trusted-access-for-cyber/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">申请网络安全可信访问权限（Trusted Access for Cyber）（需联网）</a>。使用 ChatGPT 身份验证的个人可以使用<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/cyber\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">个人可信访问流程（需联网）</a>。部分账户或代码仓库执行全仓库扫描时需要此权限。</li> <li>GitLab Ultimate 19.2 或更高版本，以支持<a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/user/application_security/detect/sarif/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">接收 SARIF 2.1.0（需联网）</a>。</li> <li>完整的 Git 历史记录，以便合并请求作业计算合并基点。</li> </ul> <p>流水线镜像会安装 Node.js 26、Python 3、Git、<code>rg</code> 和固定版本的 Codex Security CLI。自动修复还需要现有的回归测试，以及一个能够在没有受保护凭据的情况下运行代码仓库控制命令的运行器。</p> <p><a id=\"start-with-a-scan-only-pipeline\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">从只扫描的流水线开始</h2> <p>创建一个已遮蔽、隐藏并受保护的 GitLab CI/CD 变量，命名为 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code>。使用具有 Codex Security 访问权限的 OpenAI Platform API 密钥，并将其环境范围设为 <code>codex-security/openai</code>。请参阅<a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/ci/environments/#limit-the-environment-scope-of-a-cicd-variable\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">设置 CI/CD 变量的环境范围（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>先将此流水线加入测试项目。它会扫描符合条件且分支受保护的合并请求中已提交的变更，在成功的报告作业中发布 SARIF，并在单独的门禁作业中恢复扫描器的结果：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">stages:\n  - security_scan\n  - security_gate\n\n.codex-security-merge-request:\n  rules:\n    - if: '$CI_PIPELINE_SOURCE == \"merge_request_event\" &amp;&amp; $CI_MERGE_REQUEST_SOURCE_PROJECT_ID == $CI_PROJECT_ID &amp;&amp; $CI_MERGE_REQUEST_SOURCE_BRANCH_PROTECTED == \"true\" &amp;&amp; $CI_MERGE_REQUEST_TARGET_BRANCH_PROTECTED == \"true\"'\n\ncodex-security:\n  extends: .codex-security-merge-request\n  stage: security_scan\n  image: node:26-bookworm-slim\n  environment:\n    name: codex-security/openai\n    action: access\n  variables:\n    GIT_DEPTH: \"0\"\n  before_script:\n    - apt-get update -qq\n    - apt-get install -y -qq --no-install-recommends ca-certificates git python3 ripgrep\n    - npm install --prefix /tmp/codex-security-cli --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund @openai/codex-security@0.1.20\n  script:\n    - |\n      set -eu\n      test -n \"${CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY:-}\"\n\n      CODEX_SECURITY_BIN=\"/tmp/codex-security-cli/node_modules/.bin/codex-security\"\n      RESULTS_DIR=\"/tmp/codex-security-results-$CI_JOB_ID\"\n      ARTIFACT_DIR=\"codex-security-artifacts\"\n      BASE_REVISION=\"$(git merge-base \\\n        \"$CI_MERGE_REQUEST_DIFF_BASE_SHA\" \"$CI_COMMIT_SHA\")\"\n      install -d -m 700 \"$RESULTS_DIR\" \"$ARTIFACT_DIR/results\"\n\n      codex_security_api_key=\"$CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY\"\n      unset CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY\n      set +e\n      OPENAI_API_KEY=\"$codex_security_api_key\" \\\n        \"$CODEX_SECURITY_BIN\" scan . \\\n          --diff \"$BASE_REVISION\" \\\n          --head \"$CI_COMMIT_SHA\" \\\n          --auth api-key \\\n          --output-dir \"$RESULTS_DIR\" \\\n          --json\n      scan_exit=\"$?\"\n      set -e\n      unset codex_security_api_key\n\n      case \"$scan_exit\" in\n        0|1|2) ;;\n        *) exit \"$scan_exit\" ;;\n      esac\n\n      \"$CODEX_SECURITY_BIN\" export \"$RESULTS_DIR\" \\\n        --export-format sarif \\\n        --source-root \"$CI_PROJECT_DIR\" \\\n        --output \"$ARTIFACT_DIR/results.sarif\"\n      test -s \"$ARTIFACT_DIR/results.sarif\"\n      cp -R \"$RESULTS_DIR\"/. \"$ARTIFACT_DIR/results/\"\n      printf '%s\\n' \"$scan_exit\" &gt; \"$ARTIFACT_DIR/scan-exit-code.txt\"\n      exit 0\n  artifacts:\n    when: always\n    access: maintainer\n    expire_in: 7 days\n    paths:\n      - codex-security-artifacts/\n    reports:\n      sarif: codex-security-artifacts/results.sarif\n\ncodex-security-gate:\n  extends: .codex-security-merge-request\n  stage: security_gate\n  image: alpine:3.20\n  needs:\n    - job: codex-security\n      artifacts: true\n  script:\n    - exit \"$(cat codex-security-artifacts/scan-exit-code.txt)\"\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>插图：GitLab 流水线扫描已提交的差异、发布 SARIF 报告，并在策略门禁中恢复扫描结果。</p> </blockquote> <p>运行使用机密的作业之前，请检查 <code>.gitlab-ci.yml</code> 中的每一项变更。此示例不包含全仓库扫描或自动修复。</p> <p><a id=\"adopt-the-production-pipeline\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">采用生产流水线</h2> <ol> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/security/cli/ci/gitlab.yml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">下载完整的 GitLab 流水线（本地尚未收录）</a>，并将其保存为代码仓库根目录中的 <code>.gitlab-ci.yml</code>。如果代码仓库已有流水线，请将示例中的阶段、隐藏模板和作业合并到现有文件中。</li> <li>保留现有的构建、测试和部署阶段。如果项目使用 <code>workflow: rules</code>，请确认这些规则允许你希望扫描的流水线事件。</li> </ol> <p>示例新增了 <code>security_scan</code>、<code>security_remediation</code>、<code>security_publish</code> 和 <code>security_gate</code> 阶段。只生成扫描报告时，只需要 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code>。</p> <p>默认情况下，扫描作业只会针对同一项目内、两个受保护分支之间的合并请求运行。若要扫描受保护默认分支上的推送和手动流水线，请设置 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_FULL_SCAN_DEFAULT_BRANCH=true</code>。若要启用受保护默认分支上的定时深度扫描，请设置 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_SCHEDULED_DEEP_SCAN=true</code>，并明确配置时间和费用预算。</p> <p>只有符合以下条件时，合并请求流水线才能访问受保护变量和运行器：</p> <ul> <li>在同一项目中保护源分支和目标分支。</li> <li>项目<a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/ci/pipelines/merge_request_pipelines/#control-access-to-protected-variables-and-runners\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">允许合并请求流水线访问受保护变量和运行器（需联网）</a>。</li> <li>启动流水线的用户有权限推送到目标分支或将变更合并到目标分支。</li> </ul> <p>Fork 流水线和未受保护的合并请求无法获得扫描凭据。在运行使用机密的作业之前，请检查 <code>.gitlab-ci.yml</code> 中的每一项变更。遮蔽或隐藏变量，并不能让不可信的 CI 代码变得安全。</p> <p><a id=\"run-a-scan-and-review-findings\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">运行扫描并查看发现项</h2> <p>创建符合条件的受保护合并请求，或在受保护的默认分支上运行流水线。运行需要付费的全仓库扫描之前，建议先从较小的差异开始。</p> <p>打开 <code>codex-security</code> 作业，并确认其产物包含：</p> <ul> <li><code>scan-manifest.json</code></li> <li><code>findings.json</code></li> <li><code>coverage.json</code></li> <li><code>results.sarif</code></li> <li><code>scan-exit-code.txt</code></li> </ul> <p>然后打开流水线的 <strong>Security</strong> 选项卡，查看接收警告，并确认发现项标识符、严重级别和源代码位置。默认分支扫描还会创建项目级漏洞记录。合并请求中的发现项会显示在流水线的 Security 选项卡或合并请求安全小组件中，但不会创建项目范围的漏洞记录。</p> <p>扫描结果可能包含存在漏洞的源代码片段、证据和修复详情，因此请限制产物的访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-scan-profile\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">选择扫描配置</h2> <p>流水线会根据触发方式选择扫描配置：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>触发方式</th> <th>扫描目标</th> <th>模式</th> <th>推理强度</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>同一项目中受保护的合并请求</td> <td>已提交的差异</td> <td><code>standard</code></td> <td><code>low</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>选择启用的受保护默认分支推送或手动触发</td> <td>整个代码仓库</td> <td><code>standard</code></td> <td><code>high</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>受保护默认分支上的选择启用的定时任务</td> <td>整个代码仓库</td> <td><code>deep</code></td> <td><code>xhigh</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>合并请求扫描重点检查已提交的变更，以便提供针对性反馈。默认分支扫描会检查已集成的代码仓库。定时深度扫描提供更广泛的周期性覆盖。一次已完成的差异扫描只适用于该次变更，不能证明整个代码仓库都没有问题。</p> <p>该工作流程会在代码仓库之外安装 CLI，并通过绝对路径运行。试运行预检会使用仅供当前进程读取的 API 密钥，但不会启动付费扫描，也不会验证 API 身份验证、Codex Security 访问权限、配额或模型可用性。</p> <p>工作流程会将扫描状态和结果写到工作树之外，并将 <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> 的作用范围限制在扫描进程中。CLI 接收的是明确列出的少量环境变量，而不会继承 GitLab 的全部变量。对于差异扫描，工作流程会计算合并基点，并将扫描绑定到审核过的 base 和 head 修订版本。</p> <p>示例将 <code>@openai/codex-security</code> 固定在 <code>0.1.20</code>。更改此固定版本前，请重新测试身份验证、产物、SARIF 接收和策略门禁。</p> <p><a id=\"separate-reporting-from-policy-enforcement\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">将报告与策略执行分开</h2> <p>GitLab 会从成功的报告作业中接收 SARIF。流水线先发布报告，再在单独的 <code>codex-security-gate</code> 作业中恢复扫描器的退出状态。</p> <p>报告作业接受退出码 <code>0</code> 和 <code>1</code> 下的发现项。只有当扫描清单证明扫描已完成、覆盖情况明确标记为 <code>partial</code>，并且存在非空 SARIF 报告时，它才接受退出码 <code>2</code>。其他运行时、配置或导出错误仍会阻止流水线继续。</p> <p>最终门禁会保留扫描器的以下退出码：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>退出码</th> <th>含义</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>0</code></td> <td>扫描已完成，覆盖完整，并通过相应策略。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>1</code></td> <td>扫描已完成，并发现达到或超过配置阈值的问题。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>2</code></td> <td>扫描覆盖不完整，或发生输入错误或运行时错误。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>校准部分覆盖行为期间，示例会暂时允许退出码 <code>2</code>。当覆盖不完整必须阻止流水线时，请移除该放行设置。</p> <p>修复和发布步骤会在最终策略门禁之前运行。即使门禁最终令流水线失败，符合条件的发现项仍可以生成一份已验证的草稿合并请求。</p> <p><a id=\"enable-verified-remediation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">启用已验证的自动修复</h2> <p>自动修复是可选功能，只会在受保护默认分支的流水线中运行。Codex 修复进程和由代码仓库控制的验证命令，不会获得 GitLab 项目访问令牌或运行器注入的凭据。</p> <p>该工作流程会：</p> <ol> <li>要求扫描覆盖完整，并且发现项严重级别为 <code>high</code> 或 <code>critical</code>。</li> <li>确认配置的回归测试在修复之前会失败。</li> <li>生成补丁，并拒绝修改 CI、凭据、二进制文件或其他受保护文件。</li> <li>在不提供 OpenAI、GitLab、注册表、部署或作业令牌凭据的情况下运行回归测试。</li> <li>使用 <code>verify-fix</code> 返回 <code>fixed</code>、<code>still_vulnerable</code> 或 <code>inconclusive</code>。只有当 <code>verify-fix</code> 返回 <code>fixed</code>，且验证进程没有更改补丁时，作业才会发布补丁。</li> </ol> <p>设置以下受保护变量，以启用自动修复：</p> <ul> <li>将 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_ENABLE_REMEDIATION</code> 设为 <code>true</code>。</li> <li>将 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_VERIFICATION_COMMAND</code> 设为现有回归测试；修复前应以 <code>1</code> 退出，修复后应以 <code>0</code> 退出。</li> <li>可以选择将 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_SETUP_COMMAND</code> 设为一条非交互式依赖安装命令。</li> </ul> <p>选择能够验证底层安全不变量的回归测试，而不是仅针对某种具体实现的测试。对于生成的测试和源代码变更，也应采用同样严格的审查标准。</p> <details> <summary>高级内容：隔离代码仓库命令</summary> <code>validate</code>、<code>patch</code> 和 <code>verify-fix</code> 命令会接收仅供当前进程读取的 <code>CODEX_API_KEY</code>。由代码仓库控制的设置和测试命令，会以单独的非特权用户身份在已跟踪源文件的可写副本中运行。该副本不包含 Git 元数据、子模块内容和下载的产物。需要 <code>.git</code> 或子模块的设置和测试命令，必须放在单独设计且不含凭据的作业中运行。 只有由 root 管理的 Codex 步骤可以访问规范检出目录或 GitLab 相邻的文件变量目录。副本中的干净环境只包含 <code>PATH</code>、<code>HOME</code>、<code>LANG</code>、<code>CI</code> 和 <code>CI_PROJECT_DIR</code>。如果命令需要其他非机密值，请先审核该命令，再将所需变量加入允许列表。如果运行器无法切换用户，请先将验证步骤移到不含凭据的独立作业中，然后再启用自动修复。 </details> <p><a id=\"publish-a-draft-merge-request\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">发布草稿合并请求</h2> <p>创建一个 <a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/user/project/settings/project_access_tokens/#create-a-project-access-token\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitLab 项目访问令牌（需联网）</a>，并授予 Developer 角色及 <code>api</code>、<code>write_repository</code> 范围。将它保存为受保护、已遮蔽且隐藏的 <code>GITLAB_REMEDIATION_TOKEN</code>，并将范围仅限于 <code>codex-security/publish</code> 环境。</p> <p>将 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_CREATE_MR=true</code> 设为启用发布功能。还要将非机密变量 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_MR_TEST_COMMAND</code> 设为项目专用的安全回归测试；每个生成的修复分支都必须通过该测试。请将此变量设为非受保护状态，以便生成的非受保护合并请求可以读取该命令。发布工作流程会：</p> <ul> <li>接收代码仓库写入令牌，但不会获得 OpenAI 凭据。</li> <li>创建 <code>codex-security/fix-&lt;finding-hash&gt;</code> 分支。</li> <li>创建草稿合并请求；如果已存在未关闭的草稿，则复用它，而不是重复创建。</li> <li>以非特权用户身份，在仅包含已跟踪文件且不含受保护凭据的副本中运行非受保护修复分支的回归测试。</li> <li>绝不会自动合并生成的变更。</li> </ul> <p>不要用 <code>CI_JOB_TOKEN</code> 替代项目访问令牌；它无法执行创建合并请求所需的操作。合并之前，请审核拟议补丁、验证证据和发现项。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-optional-variables\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">配置可选变量</h2> <p>只配置你实际启用的功能所需变量：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>变量</th> <th>用途</th> <th>默认值或说明</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code></td> <td>每次扫描</td> <td>受保护、已遮蔽、隐藏；范围限定为 <code>codex-security/openai</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_VERSION</code></td> <td>升级 CLI</td> <td>固定为 <code>0.1.20</code>；更改前重新测试</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_FULL_SCAN_DEFAULT_BRANCH</code></td> <td>默认分支全仓库扫描</td> <td>明确选择启用；默认关闭</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_SCHEDULED_DEEP_SCAN</code></td> <td>定时深度扫描</td> <td>明确选择启用；默认关闭</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_DEEP_MAX_TIME_HOURS</code></td> <td>定时深度扫描</td> <td>必需的时间预算，大于 <code>0</code> 且小于 <code>8</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_DEEP_MAX_COST</code></td> <td>定时深度扫描</td> <td>必需的美元预估费用上限，大于 <code>0</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_ENABLE_REMEDIATION</code></td> <td>生成补丁</td> <td>受保护的选择启用项；默认关闭</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_VERIFICATION_COMMAND</code></td> <td>生成补丁</td> <td>受保护的回归测试</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_SETUP_COMMAND</code></td> <td>可选的修复设置</td> <td>受保护的依赖安装命令</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_REMEDIATION_EFFORT</code></td> <td>可选的修复调优</td> <td><code>high</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_MAX_CHANGED_FILES</code></td> <td>可选的补丁大小限制</td> <td><code>8</code>；允许范围为 <code>1</code> 到 <code>20</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_CREATE_MR</code></td> <td>创建草稿合并请求</td> <td>受保护的选择启用项；默认关闭</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>GITLAB_REMEDIATION_TOKEN</code></td> <td>创建草稿合并请求</td> <td>范围限定为 <code>codex-security/publish</code> 的 Developer 项目令牌</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_GITLAB_INTERNAL_URL</code></td> <td>可选的自托管发布</td> <td>运行器可访问的 GitLab 源站</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_MR_TEST_COMMAND</code></td> <td>发布草稿合并请求</td> <td>必需的非机密、项目专用回归测试</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_MR_SETUP_COMMAND</code></td> <td>可选的修复分支设置</td> <td>非机密的依赖设置命令</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>GitLab 会提供 <code>CI_*</code> 变量。流水线会管理 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_BIN</code>、<code>CODEX_SECURITY_EFFORT</code>、<code>CODEX_SECURITY_MODE</code>、<code>CODEX_SECURITY_STATE_DIR</code> 和 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_TARGET</code>；不要将它们配置为项目变量。对于差异扫描，CLI 会根据标准化后的 base 和 head 修订版本计算规范目标标识。</p> <p><a id=\"tune-enforcement-and-cost\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">调整策略和费用限制</h2> <p>合并请求反馈使用差异扫描，默认分支使用标准全仓库扫描，定时深度扫描则提供更广泛的覆盖。默认情况下，两种全仓库扫描配置都处于关闭状态。定时深度扫描还要求设置 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_DEEP_MAX_TIME_HOURS</code> 和 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_DEEP_MAX_COST</code>；CLI 的时间预算应短于作业的 8 小时超时限制。设定预算前，请测量具有代表性的运行情况。<code>--max-cost</code> 是预估费用保护值，不是硬性账单上限。</p> <p>先运行只生成报告的扫描。团队检查有代表性的发现项、覆盖范围、费用和运行时间后，再添加 <code>--fail-on-severity</code>。有关严重级别策略，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99?anchor=choose-a-severity-policy\">CI/CD 概览</a>；有关退出代码，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=exit-codes-and-signals\">CLI 参考</a>。</p> <p>作业失败时：</p> <ul> <li>扫描产物缺失通常表示配置或运行器存在问题。</li> <li>如果已有产物但覆盖不完整，请检查 <code>coverage.json</code>。</li> <li>如果 GitLab 没有显示发现项，请检查 SARIF 报告作业是否成功，以及 GitLab 是否接受了报告。</li> <li>如果跳过自动修复，请检查受保护分支、覆盖完整性、发现项严重级别、验证命令和选择启用的变量。</li> <li>如果发布失败，请检查项目令牌的角色、范围和环境限制。</li> </ul> <p>所有命令、标志和产物请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34\">Codex Security CLI 参考</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"run-codex-security-in-gitlab-cicd\">Run Codex Security in GitLab CI/CD</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Run Codex Security in GitLab CI/CD to scan committed changes and protected branches, publish findings to GitLab Security, and optionally propose verified fixes in draft merge requests.</p> <p>The workflow keeps scan credentials separate from repository-write access. Generated changes always require human review before merge.</p> <p>Start with scan-only reporting. Enable remediation only after you check the runner, findings, and credential boundaries for your project.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-begin\">Before you begin</h2> <p>You need:</p> <ul> <li>A GitLab project with a trusted runner that supports the Codex sandbox's user namespace.</li> <li>The Maintainer or Owner role in the GitLab project so you can configure <a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/ci/variables/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">project CI/CD variables (online)</a> and protected resources.</li> <li>An OpenAI API key with Codex Security access. Organizations using Platform API keys can <a href=\"https://openai.com/form/enterprise-trusted-access-for-cyber/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">request Trusted Access for Cyber (online)</a>. Individuals using ChatGPT authentication can use the <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/cyber\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">personal Trusted Access flow (online)</a>. Some accounts or repositories require this access for full-repository scans.</li> <li>GitLab Ultimate 19.2 or later for <a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/user/application_security/detect/sarif/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SARIF 2.1.0 ingestion (online)</a>.</li> <li>Full Git history so merge request jobs can calculate the merge base.</li> </ul> <p>The pipeline image installs Node.js 26, Python 3, Git, <code>rg</code>, and the pinned Codex Security CLI. Automated remediation additionally requires an existing regression test and a runner that can run repository-controlled commands without protected credentials.</p> <h2 id=\"start-with-a-scan-only-pipeline\">Start with a scan-only pipeline</h2> <p>Create a masked, hidden, protected GitLab CI/CD variable named <code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code>. Use an OpenAI Platform API key with Codex Security access, and set its environment scope to <code>codex-security/openai</code>. See <a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/ci/environments/#limit-the-environment-scope-of-a-cicd-variable\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">environment-scoped CI/CD variables (online)</a>.</p> <p>Add this pipeline to a test project first. It scans committed changes in eligible protected merge requests, publishes SARIF from a successful report job, and restores the scanner result in a separate gate:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">stages:\n  - security_scan\n  - security_gate\n\n.codex-security-merge-request:\n  rules:\n    - if: '$CI_PIPELINE_SOURCE == \"merge_request_event\" &amp;&amp; $CI_MERGE_REQUEST_SOURCE_PROJECT_ID == $CI_PROJECT_ID &amp;&amp; $CI_MERGE_REQUEST_SOURCE_BRANCH_PROTECTED == \"true\" &amp;&amp; $CI_MERGE_REQUEST_TARGET_BRANCH_PROTECTED == \"true\"'\n\ncodex-security:\n  extends: .codex-security-merge-request\n  stage: security_scan\n  image: node:26-bookworm-slim\n  environment:\n    name: codex-security/openai\n    action: access\n  variables:\n    GIT_DEPTH: \"0\"\n  before_script:\n    - apt-get update -qq\n    - apt-get install -y -qq --no-install-recommends ca-certificates git python3 ripgrep\n    - npm install --prefix /tmp/codex-security-cli --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund @openai/codex-security@0.1.20\n  script:\n    - |\n      set -eu\n      test -n \"${CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY:-}\"\n\n      CODEX_SECURITY_BIN=\"/tmp/codex-security-cli/node_modules/.bin/codex-security\"\n      RESULTS_DIR=\"/tmp/codex-security-results-$CI_JOB_ID\"\n      ARTIFACT_DIR=\"codex-security-artifacts\"\n      BASE_REVISION=\"$(git merge-base \\\n        \"$CI_MERGE_REQUEST_DIFF_BASE_SHA\" \"$CI_COMMIT_SHA\")\"\n      install -d -m 700 \"$RESULTS_DIR\" \"$ARTIFACT_DIR/results\"\n\n      codex_security_api_key=\"$CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY\"\n      unset CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY\n      set +e\n      OPENAI_API_KEY=\"$codex_security_api_key\" \\\n        \"$CODEX_SECURITY_BIN\" scan . \\\n          --diff \"$BASE_REVISION\" \\\n          --head \"$CI_COMMIT_SHA\" \\\n          --auth api-key \\\n          --output-dir \"$RESULTS_DIR\" \\\n          --json\n      scan_exit=\"$?\"\n      set -e\n      unset codex_security_api_key\n\n      case \"$scan_exit\" in\n        0|1|2) ;;\n        *) exit \"$scan_exit\" ;;\n      esac\n\n      \"$CODEX_SECURITY_BIN\" export \"$RESULTS_DIR\" \\\n        --export-format sarif \\\n        --source-root \"$CI_PROJECT_DIR\" \\\n        --output \"$ARTIFACT_DIR/results.sarif\"\n      test -s \"$ARTIFACT_DIR/results.sarif\"\n      cp -R \"$RESULTS_DIR\"/. \"$ARTIFACT_DIR/results/\"\n      printf '%s\\n' \"$scan_exit\" &gt; \"$ARTIFACT_DIR/scan-exit-code.txt\"\n      exit 0\n  artifacts:\n    when: always\n    access: maintainer\n    expire_in: 7 days\n    paths:\n      - codex-security-artifacts/\n    reports:\n      sarif: codex-security-artifacts/results.sarif\n\ncodex-security-gate:\n  extends: .codex-security-merge-request\n  stage: security_gate\n  image: alpine:3.20\n  needs:\n    - job: codex-security\n      artifacts: true\n  script:\n    - exit \"$(cat codex-security-artifacts/scan-exit-code.txt)\"\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: GitLab pipeline scans a committed diff, publishes a SARIF report, and restores the scan result in a policy gate</p> </blockquote> <p>Review every change to <code>.gitlab-ci.yml</code> before running a secret-bearing job. This example omits full scans and remediation.</p> <h2 id=\"adopt-the-production-pipeline\">Adopt the production pipeline</h2> <ol> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/security/cli/ci/gitlab.yml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Download the complete GitLab pipeline (not in this local snapshot)</a> and save it as <code>.gitlab-ci.yml</code> in the repository root. If your repository already has a pipeline, merge the example's stages, hidden templates, and jobs into the existing file.</li> <li>Preserve existing build, test, and deployment stages. If the project uses <code>workflow: rules</code>, confirm that it allows the pipeline events you want to scan.</li> </ol> <p>The example adds <code>security_scan</code>, <code>security_remediation</code>, <code>security_publish</code>, and <code>security_gate</code> stages. Scan-only reporting requires only <code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code>.</p> <p>The scan job runs by default only for same-project merge requests between protected branches. Set <code>CODEX_SECURITY_FULL_SCAN_DEFAULT_BRANCH=true</code> to scan protected default-branch pushes and manual pipelines. Set <code>CODEX_SECURITY_SCHEDULED_DEEP_SCAN=true</code> and configure explicit time and cost budgets to enable scheduled deep scans on the protected default branch.</p> <p>A merge request pipeline can access protected variables and runners only when:</p> <ul> <li>You protect the source and target branches in the same project.</li> <li>The project <a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/ci/pipelines/merge_request_pipelines/#control-access-to-protected-variables-and-runners\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">permits merge request pipelines to access protected variables and runners (online)</a>.</li> <li>The user who starts the pipeline can push or merge into the target branch.</li> </ul> <p>Fork pipelines and unprotected merge requests don't receive the scan credential. Review every change to <code>.gitlab-ci.yml</code> before running a secret-bearing job. Masking and hiding a variable do not make untrusted CI code safe.</p> <h2 id=\"run-a-scan-and-review-findings\">Run a scan and review findings</h2> <p>Create an eligible protected merge request or run the pipeline on the protected default branch. Start with a small diff before running a paid full-repository scan.</p> <p>Open the <code>codex-security</code> job and confirm that its artifacts include:</p> <ul> <li><code>scan-manifest.json</code></li> <li><code>findings.json</code></li> <li><code>coverage.json</code></li> <li><code>results.sarif</code></li> <li><code>scan-exit-code.txt</code></li> </ul> <p>Then open the pipeline <strong>Security</strong> tab, review ingestion warnings, and confirm finding identifiers, severity levels, and source locations. Default-branch scans also create project vulnerability records. Merge request findings appear in the pipeline Security tab or merge request security widget but don't create project-wide vulnerability records.</p> <p>Restrict artifact access because scan results can contain vulnerable source snippets, evidence, and remediation details.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-a-scan-profile\">Choose a scan profile</h2> <p>The pipeline selects a profile from the trigger:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Trigger</th> <th>Target</th> <th>Mode</th> <th>Effort</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Protected same-project merge request</td> <td>Committed diff</td> <td><code>standard</code></td> <td><code>low</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Opt-in protected default-branch push or manual</td> <td>Full repository</td> <td><code>standard</code></td> <td><code>high</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Opt-in schedule on protected default branch</td> <td>Full repository</td> <td><code>deep</code></td> <td><code>xhigh</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Merge request scans focus feedback on the committed change. Default-branch scans review the integrated repository. Scheduled deep scans provide broader periodic coverage. A completed diff scan applies only to that change and does not show that the entire repository is clean.</p> <p>The workflow installs the CLI outside the repository and runs it by absolute path. Its dry-run preflight uses the process-scoped API key but does not start a paid scan or verify API authentication, Codex Security access, quota, or model availability.</p> <p>The workflow writes scan state and results outside the worktree and scopes <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> to the scan process. The CLI receives a small, explicit environment instead of inheriting every GitLab variable. For diff scans, the workflow calculates the merge base and binds the scan to the reviewed base and head revisions.</p> <p>The example pins <code>@openai/codex-security</code> to <code>0.1.20</code>. Retest authentication, artifacts, SARIF ingestion, and policy gating before changing the pin.</p> <h2 id=\"separate-reporting-from-policy-enforcement\">Separate reporting from policy enforcement</h2> <p>GitLab ingests SARIF from a successful report job. The pipeline publishes the report first and restores the scanner's exit status in a separate <code>codex-security-gate</code> job.</p> <p>The report job accepts findings from exit codes <code>0</code> and <code>1</code>. It accepts exit code <code>2</code> only when the scan manifest proves the scan completed, coverage is explicitly <code>partial</code>, and a non-empty SARIF report exists. Other runtime, configuration, or export failures remain blocking.</p> <p>The final gate preserves these scanner exit codes:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Exit</th> <th>Meaning</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>0</code></td> <td>The scan completed with complete coverage and passed its policy.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>1</code></td> <td>The scan completed and found an issue at or above the configured threshold.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>2</code></td> <td>The scan had incomplete coverage or an input or runtime error.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>The example temporarily allows exit <code>2</code> while you calibrate partial coverage. Remove that allowance when incomplete coverage must block the pipeline.</p> <p>Remediation and publishing run before the final policy gate. An eligible finding can produce a verified draft merge request even when the gate later fails the pipeline.</p> <h2 id=\"enable-verified-remediation\">Enable verified remediation</h2> <p>Automated remediation is optional and runs only for protected default-branch pipelines. The Codex remediation process and repository-controlled verification commands do not receive the GitLab project access token or runner-injected credentials.</p> <p>The workflow:</p> <ol> <li>Requires complete scan coverage and a <code>high</code>- or <code>critical</code>-severity finding.</li> <li>Confirms that the configured regression test fails before patching.</li> <li>Generates a patch and rejects changes to CI, credential, binary, or other protected files.</li> <li>Runs the regression test without OpenAI, GitLab, registry, deployment, or job-token credentials.</li> <li>Uses <code>verify-fix</code> to return <code>fixed</code>, <code>still_vulnerable</code>, or <code>inconclusive</code>. The job publishes a patch only when <code>verify-fix</code> returns <code>fixed</code> and the verification process leaves the patch unchanged.</li> </ol> <p>Set these protected variables to enable remediation:</p> <ul> <li>Set <code>CODEX_SECURITY_ENABLE_REMEDIATION</code> to <code>true</code>.</li> <li>Set <code>CODEX_SECURITY_VERIFICATION_COMMAND</code> to an existing regression test that exits <code>1</code> before the fix and <code>0</code> afterward.</li> <li>Optionally, set <code>CODEX_SECURITY_SETUP_COMMAND</code> to a non-interactive dependency setup command.</li> </ul> <p>Choose a regression test that exercises the underlying security invariant, not a particular implementation. Apply the same scrutiny to generated test and source changes.</p> <details> <summary>Advanced: repository command isolation</summary> The <code>validate</code>, <code>patch</code>, and <code>verify-fix</code> commands receive a process-scoped <code>CODEX_API_KEY</code>. Repository-controlled setup and test commands run as a separate unprivileged user in a writable copy of the tracked source files. The copy excludes Git metadata, submodule contents, and downloaded artifacts. Setup and test commands that require <code>.git</code> or submodules must run in a separately designed credential-free job. Only the root-owned Codex steps can access the canonical checkout or GitLab's adjacent file-variable directory. The copy's clean environment contains only <code>PATH</code>, <code>HOME</code>, <code>LANG</code>, <code>CI</code>, and <code>CI_PROJECT_DIR</code>. If a command needs another non-secret value, add it to the allowlist after reviewing the command. If your runner cannot change users, move verification into a separate credential-free job before enabling remediation. </details> <h2 id=\"publish-a-draft-merge-request\">Publish a draft merge request</h2> <p>Create a <a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/user/project/settings/project_access_tokens/#create-a-project-access-token\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitLab project access token (online)</a> with the Developer role and the <code>api</code> and <code>write_repository</code> scopes. Store it as a protected, masked, hidden <code>GITLAB_REMEDIATION_TOKEN</code> scoped only to the <code>codex-security/publish</code> environment.</p> <p>Set <code>CODEX_SECURITY_CREATE_MR=true</code> to enable publishing. Also set the non-secret <code>CODEX_SECURITY_MR_TEST_COMMAND</code> to the project-specific security regression test that every generated remediation branch must pass. Keep this variable unprotected so the generated unprotected merge request can read the command. The publishing workflow:</p> <ul> <li>Receives the repository-write token but no OpenAI credential.</li> <li>Creates a <code>codex-security/fix-&lt;finding-hash&gt;</code> branch.</li> <li>Opens a draft merge request and reuses an existing open draft instead of creating a duplicate.</li> <li>Runs the unprotected remediation branch's regression test as an unprivileged user in a tracked-only copy without protected credentials.</li> <li>Never merges the generated change automatically.</li> </ul> <p>Don't substitute <code>CI_JOB_TOKEN</code> for the project access token. It cannot perform the required merge request creation operation. Review the proposed patch, verification evidence, and finding before merging.</p> <h2 id=\"configure-optional-variables\">Configure optional variables</h2> <p>Configure only the variables needed for the features you enable:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Variable</th> <th>When needed</th> <th>Default or purpose</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_API_KEY</code></td> <td>Every scan</td> <td>Protected, masked, hidden; scope to <code>codex-security/openai</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_VERSION</code></td> <td>CLI upgrade</td> <td>Pinned to <code>0.1.20</code>; retest before changing</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_FULL_SCAN_DEFAULT_BRANCH</code></td> <td>Default-branch full scans</td> <td>Explicit opt-in; off by default</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_SCHEDULED_DEEP_SCAN</code></td> <td>Scheduled deep scans</td> <td>Explicit opt-in; off by default</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_DEEP_MAX_TIME_HOURS</code></td> <td>Scheduled deep scans</td> <td>Required time budget greater than <code>0</code> and less than <code>8</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_DEEP_MAX_COST</code></td> <td>Scheduled deep scans</td> <td>Required estimated USD cost guardrail greater than <code>0</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_ENABLE_REMEDIATION</code></td> <td>Patch generation</td> <td>Protected opt-in; off by default</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_VERIFICATION_COMMAND</code></td> <td>Patch generation</td> <td>Protected regression test</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_SETUP_COMMAND</code></td> <td>Optional remediation setup</td> <td>Protected dependency installation</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_REMEDIATION_EFFORT</code></td> <td>Optional remediation tuning</td> <td><code>high</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_MAX_CHANGED_FILES</code></td> <td>Optional patch-size limit</td> <td><code>8</code>; allowed range <code>1</code> through <code>20</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_CREATE_MR</code></td> <td>Draft merge request creation</td> <td>Protected opt-in; off by default</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>GITLAB_REMEDIATION_TOKEN</code></td> <td>Draft merge request creation</td> <td>Developer project token scoped to <code>codex-security/publish</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_GITLAB_INTERNAL_URL</code></td> <td>Optional self-hosted publishing</td> <td>GitLab origin reachable from the runner</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_MR_TEST_COMMAND</code></td> <td>Draft merge request publishing</td> <td>Required non-secret, project-specific regression test</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>CODEX_SECURITY_MR_SETUP_COMMAND</code></td> <td>Optional remediation branch setup</td> <td>Non-secret dependency setup</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>GitLab supplies the <code>CI_*</code> variables. The pipeline manages <code>CODEX_SECURITY_BIN</code>, <code>CODEX_SECURITY_EFFORT</code>, <code>CODEX_SECURITY_MODE</code>, <code>CODEX_SECURITY_STATE_DIR</code>, and <code>CODEX_SECURITY_TARGET</code>; don't configure them as project variables. For diff scans, the CLI derives the canonical target identity from the normalized base and head revisions.</p> <h2 id=\"tune-enforcement-and-cost\">Tune enforcement and cost</h2> <p>Use diff scans for merge request feedback, standard repository scans for the default branch, and scheduled deep scans for broader coverage. Both full-repository profiles are off by default. A scheduled deep scan also requires <code>CODEX_SECURITY_DEEP_MAX_TIME_HOURS</code> and <code>CODEX_SECURITY_DEEP_MAX_COST</code>; keep the CLI time budget below the job's eight-hour timeout. Measure representative runs before setting a budget. Treat <code>--max-cost</code> as an estimated cost guardrail, not a hard billing cap.</p> <p>Start with report-only scans. Add <code>--fail-on-severity</code> after your team has reviewed representative findings, coverage, cost, and runtime. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99?anchor=choose-a-severity-policy\">CI/CD overview</a> for severity policies and the <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=exit-codes-and-signals\">CLI reference</a> for exit-code details.</p> <p>When a job fails:</p> <ul> <li>Missing scan artifacts point to a configuration or runner problem.</li> <li>Existing artifacts with partial coverage require reviewing <code>coverage.json</code>.</li> <li>Missing GitLab findings require checking whether the SARIF report job succeeded and whether GitLab accepted the report.</li> <li>Skipped remediation requires checking the protected branch, complete coverage, finding severity, verification command, and opt-in variables.</li> <li>Publishing errors require checking the project token's role, scopes, and environment restriction.</li> </ul> <p>For every command, flag, and artifact, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34\">Codex Security CLI reference</a>.</p>"};
